TI Machine-learning for capacitive energy storage polymer dielectrics: opportunities and challenges
SO PROGRESS IN MATERIALS SCIENCE
LA English
DT Review
DE Polymer dielectrics; Electrostatic capacitors; Machine-learning; High energy density; Structure-property relationship
ID HIGH-TEMPERATURE; INFORMATION-SYSTEM; RATIONAL DESIGN; NANOCOMPOSITES; DENSITY; CONSTANT; PREDICTION; ELECTRON; COMPOSITES; PROPERTY
AB Polymer dielectrics are the primary energy storage media in electrostatic capacitors, which are essential components in power electronics for advanced electrical and electronic systems. Polymer dielectrics possess ultrahigh power density and discharge rate, yet their energy density is severely limited by the strong couplings between properties. Many traditional strategies based on manual search and analysis have been attempted, while the progress is still suppressed due to the insufficient understanding of the structure-property relationships. Machine-learning has drawn increasing attention for screening/designing material structures with desired performance, and hence providing new opportunity to break the couplings between properties and remarkably improve the energy storage performance of polymer dielectrics. This review focuses on the application of machine-learning on the energy storage polymer dielectrics, beginning with the energy storage mechanisms and key parameters of polymer dielectrics, followed with the typical models of machine-learning accompanied with their characteristics. Then, machine-learning based researches about the coupled properties of polymers and polymer-based composites are respectively reviewed, emphasizing the structure-property relationships revealed by machinelearning model. Finally, the future direction of the machine-learning driven research on energy storage polymer dielectrics are proposed.
