TI A review on the impact mechanical behavior of fiber-reinforced polymer composites: experiments, numerical simulations and machine learning
SO COMPOSITE STRUCTURES
LA English
DT Review
DE FRPcomposites; Mechanical behavior; Impact; Numerical simulation; Machine learning
ID LOW-VELOCITY IMPACT; LAMINATED COMPOSITES; FAILURE CRITERIA; DAMAGE TOLERANCE; NEURAL-NETWORKS; PART I; TEMPERATURE; LOCALIZATION; DEFORMATION
AB Fiber-reinforced polymer (FRP) composites are widely used in aerospace and other lightweight structures because of their excellent mechanical properties. However, their limited impact damage tolerance remains a critical challenge affecting structural safety and reliability. This review systematically summarizes recent advances in the impact mechanical behavior of FRP composites from a methodological perspective, covering experimental characterization, numerical simulation, and machine learning. Advanced experimental techniques, including in situ monitoring and post-impact characterization, provide valuable insights into damage initiation and evolution. Numerical simulations based on multiscale finite element models, strain-rate-dependent constitutive formulations, and physically based failure criteria enable efficient prediction of impact responses and damage mechanisms. Machine learning further facilitates rapid impact performance prediction, damage identification, and structural optimization through data-driven approaches. Beyond summarizing recent progress, this review critically discusses the current limitations and scientific challenges of each methodology, including experimental characterization under complex service conditions, multiscale constitutive and failure modeling, and the availability, generalizability, and physical interpretability of machine learning models. Finally, emerging trends, including physics-informed machine learning, integrated intelligent frameworks, and digital twins, are highlighted as promising directions for achieving more accurate, reliable, and efficient impact assessment and design of FRP composite structures.
