   Tripathi, Ujjwal
   Batra, Rohit
TI TransChem: A hybrid transformer and cheminformatics based framework for enhanced polymer informatics
SO MATERIALS TODAY COMMUNICATIONS
LA English
DT Article
DE Polymer informatics; Polymer design; Transformers; cheminformatics; Multi-task learning; LLMs
ID MOLECULAR-DYNAMICS
AB In the past decade, numerous machine learning (ML) approaches have been developed to improve the accuracy of polymer property prediction models, enabling rapid screening of polymers with tailored properties and driving significant advances in polymer discovery. Among these, the transformer-based models such as TransPolymer have shown superior performance over other classical models by capturing complex contextual information from polymer data. However, such deep learning models often operate as "black boxes", lacking interpretability and limiting their utility to enhance chemical understanding. In contrast, classical ML models based on cheminformatics-derived features provide some level of interpretability but suffer from lower predictive accuracy and limited scalability across large chemical spaces. In this work, we introduce TransChem, a hybrid ML framework that integrates transformer architectures with cheminformatics-based descriptors to achieve state-of-the-art performance across nine out of ten benchmark polymer datasets, covering properties such as electrical, electronic, optical, and ionic conductivity. We further explore multi-task learning with TransChem framework, resulting in partial improvement in model performance. More importantly, our analysis clearly show that the integration of cheminformatics features contributes complementary and chemically meaningful information to the transformer-based model, enhancing both its predictive accuracy and interpretability. Further, feature analysis on the trained TransChem models revealed key chemical factors influencing various polymer properties, thereby highlighting the interpretability of the trained models. Thus, in contrast to the prevailing trend of developing ML models based solely on either cheminformatics or transformer architectures, the TransChem model offers a promising hybrid framework for data-driven polymer design, with potential for extension in the broader field of molecular and materials informatics.
