   Advincula, Rigoberto
TI Artificial intelligence in advanced polymer manufacturing
SO MRS COMMUNICATIONS
LA English
DT Review
DE AI; Polymer manufacturing; Machine learning; Additive manufacturing; Sustainability
ID OPTIMIZATION
AB Artificial intelligence (AI) is currently transforming the polymer lifecycle, from materials discovery and design to manufacturing and recycling processes. In this review, we will discuss the undergoing paradigm shift from conventional labor-intensive processes to machine learning and data-driven automation, including the key machine learning models and techniques being applied across diverse areas of polymer science and engineering. Significant limitations and opportunities in AI-driven polymer manufacturing exist in data availability and model interpretability.
