TI Artificial intelligence techniques in energy-storage polymer-based dielectrics: A review
SO JOURNAL OF ENERGY STORAGE
LA English
DT Review
DE Polymer-based dielectrics; Energy storage performance; Artificial intelligence; Machine learning
ID OPPORTUNITIES; DISCOVERY
AB Artificial intelligence (AI) technology is revolutionizing polymer-based dielectrics energy storage, drawing significant attention to its potential for enabling efficient design and optimizing performance. The common application forms of AI technology include machine learning (ML) algorithms and some emerging predictive learning methods. This review summarizes the energy storage mechanisms of polymer-based dielectrics and the application progress of machine learning algorithms in energy storage polymer dielectrics, focusing on dataset learning and prediction, data-driven structural design, and experimental guidance. Finally, it summarizes the impact of AI and addresses key challenges with future advancement prospects. This review is expected to provide new perspectives for the structural optimization of energy storage polymer dielectrics under the integration of materials, energy, and AI technologies.
