TI Machine learning with active pharmaceutical ingredient/polymer interaction mechanism: Prediction for complex phase behaviors of pharmaceuticals and formulations
SO CHINESE JOURNAL OF CHEMICAL ENGINEERING
LA English
DT Article
DE Multi -task machine learning; Density functional theory; Hydrogen bond interaction; Miscibility; Solubility
ID TERM PHYSICAL STABILITY; PERTURBED-CHAIN SAFT; PVP; HUMIDITY; EQUATION; STATE
AB The high throughput prediction of the thermodynamic phase behavior of active pharmaceutical ingredients (APIs) with pharmaceutically relevant excipients remains a major scientific challenge in the screening of pharmaceutical formulations. In this work, a developed machine-learning model efficiently predicts the solubility of APIs in polymers by learning the phase equilibrium principle and using a few molecular descriptors. Under the few-shot learning framework, thermodynamic theory (perturbed-chain statistical associating fluid theory) was used for data augmentation, and computational chemistry was applied for molecular descriptors' screening. The results showed that the developed machine-learning model can predict the API-polymer phase diagram accurately, broaden the solubility data of APIs in polymers, and reproduce the relationship between API solubility and the interaction mechanisms between API and polymer successfully, which provided efficient guidance for the development of pharmaceutical formulations. (c) 2023 The Chemical Industry and Engineering Society of China, and Chemical Industry Press Co., Ltd. All rights reserved.
