TI Polymer Gear Pitting Severity Diagnosis Using Vibration-Based Deep Learning Architectures
SO JOURNAL OF VIBRATION ENGINEERING & TECHNOLOGIES
LA English
DT Article
DE Polymer gears; Pitting fault diagnosis; Vibration-based condition monitoring; CNN; Bi-LSTM; Transformer
AB Purpose Polymer gears are increasingly used in lightweight and low-power transmission systems. However, due to repeated loading and creep effects, pitting may occur on the gear tooth surface. Early-stage detection of pitting is therefore crucial for ensuring the reliable operation of polymer gears.Methods This study presents an end-to-end vibration-based deep learning framework for polymer gear pitting severity classification using raw vibration signals. Four architectures, namely CNN, CNN-Attention, CNN-Bi-LSTM, and CNN-Transformer, are systematically investigated under varying operating speeds, loads, and signal segmentation strategies. A comprehensive ablation study is conducted to analyze the influence of window length on diagnostic accuracy, reliability, and computational efficiency.Results and Conclusions The results demonstrate that the proposed deep learning framework achieves high classification performance across different signal segmentation lengths. All proposed models achieve millisecond-level inference times, supporting their suitability for real-time polymer gear condition monitoring under variable operating conditions.
