TI Designing of a library of polymers and prediction of thermal conductivity: a machine assisted framework
SO JOURNAL OF PHYSICS AND CHEMISTRY OF SOLIDS
LA English
DT Article
DE Machine learning; Thermal conductivity; Visualization; Polymers
ID POLYVINYL-CHLORIDE
AB Designing polymers with desired thermal conductivity is a complex and time-consuming process. This study presents a machine-assisted framework for the designing of a diverse library of polymers and prediction of thermal conductivity. Multiple machine learning (ML) models are tried and Random Forest model is best model. 10k polymers are generated. Their thermal conductivity is predicted using best model. Thirty polymers are chosen after the generated polymers are filtered based on their predicted thermal conductivity. The framework also assesses the synthetic accessibility of the polymers, identifying candidates that are not only high-performing but also relatively easy to synthesise. This approach significantly accelerates the discovery and optimization of polymers with tailored thermal properties, offering a powerful tool for materials science and engineering applications.
